      "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp",
      "name": "Localized Blizzard",
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "sort": 200000,
      "system": {
        "_migration": {
          "previous": {
            "foundry": "13.351",
            "schema": 0.941,
            "system": "7.7.4"
          },
          "version": 0.953
        },
        "actionType": {
          "value": "passive"
        },
        "actions": {
          "value": null
        },
        "category": null,
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p>A localized blizzard follows Fjordcarver wherever he goes, which harries flying enemies. While Fjordcarver is alive, all other flying creatures in the arena must succeed at a @Check[type:acrobatics|dc:33|basic:false] check to Maneuver in Flight whenever they attempt to Fly. If the creature is not trained or better in Acrobatics, they automatically crit fail.</p><p><strong>Critical Success </strong>The creature can fly normally.</p><p><strong>Success </strong>The creature can fly at half speed.</p><p><strong>Failure </strong>The creature doesn't fly, and wastes the action.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure </strong>The creature falls.</p><p>Additionally, the battering snow makes it difficult to move one's arms. Flying and air-walking creatures in the blizzard take a -2 circumstance penalty to Strikes and must succeed at a <span style=\"font-family:var(--font-primary)\">@Check[type:flat|dc:5|basic:false] when attempting any action with the manipulate trait. On a failure, the action is lost.</span></p>"
        },
